!Name: p900-1
!C Period 900 c/3 spaceship.
!C This is the first of a series of spaceships with arbitrarily large periods.
!C The spaceship works by sending a MWSS from the back to the front, and then
!C creating a loaf which the back of the spaceship catches up to again.
!C Moving the middle c/3 spaceships forwards by 60 cells increases the period
!C by 540.  This can be repeated as desired to create a spaceship with an
!C arbitrarily high period, any one of 900 + 540N.  The feaure of this series
!C of spaceships is that the population has the same bound no matter how high
!C the period is.  This differs from most other methods of creating arbitrarily
!C large period spaceships.  This is an improvement on an earlier version
!C of this ship.
!C David I. Bell, October 2002
!Source: jslife-moving
!
